{
 "schema": 1,
 "about": "The duplicated-work count of #202: for each K class and batch count, the work a split duplicates across the kernels that write the same output element, for J and for K at the same Spec.am, and their ratio -- the arithmetic half of jengine/k-recompute-has-more-merit (claims.json), counted with no card, no compiler and no built kernel. Written by `PYTHONPATH=src uv run python -m felizjueves.eri.k_exchange.kdup --write`; recomputed by test/test_k_duplication.py (L <= 2 in the fast tier, L > 2 `slow`). It scores nothing: the claim is E3's (#207).",
 "rule": "Per primitive quartet, from plan.batching's partition and the E nonzero pattern (E^{ac}_p != 0 iff p_d <= a_d + c_d) only. Shared by J and K: the recurrence's extra FLOPs and intermediates (the sieved literal plan, plan/cost.py, at n_batches minus at one batch) and n_batches - 1 extra Boys evaluations. J: the J_p += [p+q] D_q products (partitioned by r, never duplicated) and sum_B |P_B| - n_p extra partial J_p write-backs, counted HIGH (as if per quartet). K: stage 1 (I[p] = sum_q [p|q] E^bd_q, partitioned), stage 2 (V(a,c) = sum_p E^ac_p I[p] over the p each batch holds for that (b,d) row) and stage 3 (K[a,b] += D[c,d] V(a,c) per batch with V structurally nonzero), counted LOW (nonzero terms only; no K write-back; no E re-evaluation). FLOPs: multiply-add 2, write-back 1. Duplicated = summed over batches minus the one-batch count. Direction per split cell: K>J iff K's duplicated contraction FLOPs exceed J's. Per class: supports if K>J at every admitted split, refutes if at none, cannot separate otherwise.",
 "classes": "kernel.k_spec(L): (lp, lq) = (ceil(L/2), floor(L/2)), am = (la, lc, lb, ld) bra first; the J row at the same am",
